      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p3_b1",
      "text": "and polyhedral cone constraints. This yields both practi-\ncal benefits in implementation and theoretical advantages\nin analyzing the optimization of non-convex landscapes in\nNNs. Bai et al. (2023) and Feng et al. (2024) have recently\nproposed cvxNN methods based on ADMM techniques to\nsolve high-dimensional deep learning tasks. ADMM offers\nseveral advantages, such as its robustness against hyperpa-\nrameter selection, linear decomposability for distributed op-\ntimization, and immunity to vanishing/exploding gradients.\nIts natural parallelization ability makes ADMM particularly\nsuitable for optimization in deep learning, where scalability\nis crucial. The COALA algorithm combines these features\nto effectively preference fine-tune LLMs faster with less\nmemory and compute while demonstrating competitive per-\nformance.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        69.39,
        291.18,
        246.8
